            "description": "Watch Deportes Tolima vs Club Nacional highlights and goals from CONMEBOL Libertadores on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on May 7, 2026. The stage was set for a classic CONMEBOL Libertadores encounter as two South American heavyweights collided in a match of immense tactical importance. Both teams took to the pitch with high ambitions, knowing that discipline and clinical finishing would be the deciding factors in this high-pressure environment. First Half Penalty Drama On May 7, 2026 , the match between Deportes Tolima and Club Nacional reached a fever pitch just before the interval. In a sequence of events that stunned the crowd, Club Nacional were awarded a penalty in the 45th minute, but Juan Pablo Torres failed to convert the chance, sending his effort wide. The momentum shifted instantly; moments later, Deportes Tolima earned a penalty of their own, and Luis Sandoval made no mistake, firing the ball home to give his side the lead. The emotional fallout of the opening goal led to a flurry of disciplinary actions. During a lengthy period of first-half stoppage time, yellow cards were shown to Tolima's Luis Sandoval , Brayan Rovira , and Edwar Lopez , while Sebastian Coates was booked for the visitors. The referee finally brought an end to an exhausting 59-minute opening period with the hosts holding a slim but vital advantage. Tactical Mastery and Late Goals In the second half, the game remained competitive until a series of substitutions by Deportes Tolima turned the tide decisively. In the 74th minute, the introduction of Jherson Mosquera and Jersson Gonzalez injected fresh energy into the attack. The tactical shift paid dividends almost immediately as Mosquera found the back of the net in the 78th minute, assisted by Gonzalez , effectively doubling the lead and putting the result beyond much doubt. As the clock wound down, the hosts added a final flourish to their dominant performance. In the 89th minute, Luis Sando